  "output": "The edit tool corrupted the file: the line `IFS=$'\\n'` looks correct, but the output shows a stray `\\n'` appended to the file’s end, after the `done` line. I’ll restore the file with the requested change so it has exactly seven lines:The line is changed as requested, but note an important consequence: `read <<< \"$1\"` reads only the **first line** of the argument, so with newline-delimited input only `[first]` is printed. That's inherent to `read` (unlike comma-splitting, where the whole string is one line).\n\nWorth knowing:\n\n- The first edit introduced a stray `\\n'` fragment at end of file; I rewrote the file to fix it. Current state is exactly 7 lines with `IFS=$'\\n'` on line 3 — all other lines unchanged.\n- On a truly empty first argument, `<<< \"\"` yields one empty field, so it prints `[]`.\n- If you actually want all lines split, you'd need something like `mapfile -t parts <<< \"$1\"` instead of `read` — say the word and I'll change that line only.",
